TITLE:: RCPathControl
summary:: A silent orgnsm distributing one rhythm over a batch along a path on a sphere
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCOrgnsm, Classes/RCBatch, Classes/RCRhythmDict, Classes/RCSpherePath, Classes/RCOrgnsmPatterns

DESCRIPTION::
Port of the Assemblage files' code::~orgnsm_path_control::. Once per loop it reads one rhythm from a link::Classes/RCRhythmDict::, walks a path over a spherical design (any object answering code::size::, code::triplets::, code::calcTriplets::) and hands each hit to the orgnsm of the controlled batch sitting at that point, writing every orgnsm's code::seq_list::, code::other_params_key_list:: and code::dur_params:: for the coming loop. The controlled orgnsms read the result through link::Classes/RCOrgnsmPatterns#*seqParams::.

Configurable static attributes: code::dur_params::, code::path_priority::, code::start_orgnsm_series::, code::seed_orgnsm_series::, code::orgnsm_series_pattern:: (default code::Pseq(path.mirror1, inf)::; Ref an Array in the series to hit several orgnsms at once), code::add_previous_orgnsms_to_other_params::, code::other_params_default_values::, code::path_generation_func:: (Ref'd function code::(design, start, seed)::).

The rhythm of the coming loop is held in code::staticAttrs.seqs_info:: (link::#-seqsInfo::): it is loaded from code::rhythm_dict.subseqs(path_name, path_key):: when nothing is held yet or when code::rhythm_dict::, code::path_name:: or code::path_key:: changed since the last load, and kept otherwise. What an agent writes into it between loads is what the next loop distributes: an link::Classes/RCCrawler:: on code::"static_attrs.seqs_info":: with link::Classes/RCCrawlerMoves#*nextValRhythmChange:: fades the rhythm towards its code::rhythm_dict_target:: (looked up at the same code::path_name:: / code::path_key::, see link::#-rhythmDictKeys::), while a code::path_key:: edit still switches it at once. A missing entry is reported and never held. A started control holds its rhythm right away (link::#-start::).

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: new
argument:: song
argument:: design
argument:: rhythmDict
argument:: pathName
argument:: pathKey
argument:: controlledBatch
argument:: species
argument:: tribe

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: seqsInfo
METHOD:: otherParamsKeyList
METHOD:: seqListByOrgnsm
Compile the loop and distribute its hits: batchKey → [RCSubseq].
METHOD:: setAttrsInOrgnsms

EXAMPLES::
code::
~path = RCPathControl(~song, ~tdesign, ~rhythmDict, \sampler, \test_sampler_w0, ~batch);
~pathBatch = RCBatch(\path_sampler, ~path, layerKey: \core);
~pathBatch.addCreate(~batch.name, ("dur_params": [4, 1], "quant": [4, 0]));
~pathBatch.startPrepared;
::
